# Bench position set — deterministic node-count baseline.
#
# Format: one FEN per line. Blank lines and lines beginning with '#' are ignored.
# Unlike the perft suites, lines carry no expected count: the bench total is a
# single pinned constant in the harness, not a per-position value.
#
# WHY THIS FILE IS FROZEN. The bench node count is the deterministic signal that
# distinguishes a behaviour change from a speed change. It is only meaningful if
# the inputs never move. Adding, removing, or reordering a position changes the
# total and invalidates every previously recorded number. Treat this list as
# append-only and deliberate; a change here is a change to the baseline.
#
# The set is small on purpose. Bench runs on every commit and must stay fast in
# a debug build. It spans the phases so a search change that only affects one
# phase still moves the total:
#
#   1. Initial position — the trivial baseline.
#   2. Kiwipete — dense middlegame, castling both sides, pins, many captures.
#   3. Sparse endgame — en passant and rook/pawn interaction, cheap to search deep.
#   4. Promotion under pressure — promotions and castling rights on one side.
#   5. Quiet interlocked middlegame — few captures, exercises quiet-move ordering.
#   6. Open tactical position — many checks and captures, exercises qsearch.

rnbqkbnr/pppppppp/8/8/8/8/PPPPPPPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 0 1
r3k2r/p1ppqpb1/bn2pnp1/3PN3/1p2P3/2N2Q1p/PPPBBPPP/R3K2R w KQkq - 0 1
8/2p5/3p4/KP5r/1R3p1k/8/4P1P1/8 w - - 0 1
r3k2r/Pppp1ppp/1b3nbN/nP6/BBP1P3/q4N2/Pp1P2PP/R2Q1RK1 w kq - 0 1
r4rk1/1pp1qppp/p1np1n2/2b1p1B1/2B1P1b1/P1NP1N2/1PP1QPPP/R4RK1 w - - 0 10
rnbq1k1r/pp1Pbppp/2p5/8/2B5/8/PPP1NnPP/RNBQK2R w KQ - 1 8
